Subject: [PATCH] wgl: pin opengl32.dll so pixel formats set through GDI last

opengl32.dll keeps its own record of each window's pixel format. When a
process calls ChoosePixelFormat, DescribePixelFormat or SetPixelFormat
before it has loaded opengl32.dll itself, GDI loads opengl32.dll for that
one call, opengl32.dll loads the ICD and calls DrvValidateVersion, and GDI
frees opengl32.dll again afterwards. The pixel format SetPixelFormat
recorded is lost with it. When the process loads opengl32.dll later,
GetPixelFormat returns 0 and wglCreateContext fails with
ERROR_INVALID_PIXEL_FORMAT (2000) before it calls the ICD.

GZDoom does exactly this. It loads opengl32.dll with LoadLibrary only after
it has set the pixel format of its hidden dummy window, so it could not
create its first context and stopped with "Unable to create an OpenGL
render context. Insufficient driver support for context creation".

An ICD that imports opengl32.dll keeps it loaded; this one does not.
DrvValidateVersion now pins opengl32.dll the first time it is called, so
opengl32.dll and its pixel-format records stay for the life of the process.

Evidence: docs/gzdoom.md, docs/evidence/gzdoom/ (src/gzgl.c).
Origin: vmlab-win3d gzdoom worker.
---
diff --git a/src/gallium/frontends/wgl/stw_device.c b/src/gallium/frontends/wgl/stw_device.c
index 24fd03d..dbb98c3 100644
--- a/src/gallium/frontends/wgl/stw_device.c
+++ b/src/gallium/frontends/wgl/stw_device.c
@@ -299,5 +299,27 @@ DrvValidateVersion(ULONG ulVersion)
     * ignore it.
     */
    (void)ulVersion;
+
+   /* opengl32.dll keeps its own record of each window's pixel format. When
+    * a process calls ChoosePixelFormat, DescribePixelFormat or
+    * SetPixelFormat before it has loaded opengl32.dll itself, GDI loads
+    * opengl32.dll for that one call (which loads this ICD and calls
+    * DrvValidateVersion) and frees it again afterwards. The pixel format
+    * SetPixelFormat recorded goes with it, so when the process loads
+    * opengl32.dll later, GetPixelFormat returns 0 and wglCreateContext
+    * fails with ERROR_INVALID_PIXEL_FORMAT before it reaches the ICD.
+    * GZDoom loads opengl32.dll with LoadLibrary only after setting its
+    * window's pixel format, and could not create a context.
+    *
+    * An ICD that imports opengl32.dll keeps it loaded; this one does not.
+    * Pin it the first time it loads us, so its state lives as long as the
+    * process.
+    */
+   static bool pinned;
+   if (!pinned) {
+      HMODULE opengl32;
+      pinned = GetModuleHandleExA(GET_MODULE_HANDLE_EX_FLAG_PIN, "opengl32.dll", &opengl32);
+   }
+
    return true;
 }
